    createStaticVNode('<h1 id="analytics" tabindex="-1">Analytics <a class="header-anchor" href="#analytics" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Analytics&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Analytics summarizes forms, workflows, and tasks so builders can see volume, throughput, and bottlenecks.</p><div class="tip custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Who can view</p><p>Usually available to report roles such as Admin, CEO, Manager, HR, VP. If the sidebar has no <strong>Analytics</strong> item, your role does not include reports.</p></div><h2 id="step-1-—-open-analytics" tabindex="-1">Step 1 — Open Analytics <a class="header-anchor" href="#step-1-—-open-analytics" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Step 1 — Open Analytics&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><p>In the left sidebar, under <strong>REPORTS</strong>, click <strong>Analytics</strong>.</p><p><img src="' + _imports_0 + '" alt="Analytics overview"></p></li><li><p>Wait for charts and summary cards to load.</p></li></ol><p><strong>You should see:</strong> the <strong>Analytics &amp; reports</strong> page with metrics for your organization only.</p><h2 id="step-2-—-read-the-overview" tabindex="-1">Step 2 — Read the overview <a class="header-anchor" href="#step-2-—-read-the-overview" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Step 2 — Read the overview&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Check high-level counts (executions, completions, pending work — labels match your build).</li><li>Scan charts for trends over the selected period.</li><li>Note departments or workflows that look slow or overloaded.</li></ol><h2 id="step-3-—-filter-the-view" tabindex="-1">Step 3 — Filter the view <a class="header-anchor" href="#step-3-—-filter-the-view" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Step 3 — Filter the view&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Change the <strong>date range</strong> (for example last 7 / 30 / 90 days).</li><li>Narrow by <strong>department</strong> using the picker next to it.</li><li>Re-read the charts after each filter change.</li></ol><p><strong>You should see:</strong> numbers update to match the filter — useful for monthly reviews.</p><h2 id="whose-numbers-are-these" tabindex="-1">Whose numbers are these? <a class="header-anchor" href="#whose-numbers-are-these" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Whose numbers are these?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The line under the page title says what the figures cover, because it is not the same for everyone:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>You are</th><th>The page reports on</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Admin or CEO</td><td>The whole workspace</td></tr><tr><td>Manager, HR, VP</td><td>Your team — the people who report to you</td></tr></tbody></table><p>A leader&#39;s department picker starts at <strong>My team</strong>; choosing a department narrows within that and can never show you a team you do not lead. Forms and workflow counts stay workspace-wide, since those are a shared catalogue rather than anyone&#39;s own work.</p><h2 id="step-4-—-export-if-available" tabindex="-1">Step 4 — Export (if available) <a class="header-anchor" href="#step-4-—-export-if-available" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Step 4 — Export (if available)&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Look for <strong>Export</strong> / download actions on the page header.</li><li>Download CSV or the offered format for offline reporting.</li></ol><h2 id="what-success-looks-like" tabindex="-1">What success looks like <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-success-looks-like" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What success looks like&quot;">​</a></h2><p>You can answer: “How many requests this month?”, “Where do we bottleneck?”, and “Is SLA healthy?” without opening every task.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><a href="/docs/guide/dashboard">Dashboard</a></li><li><a href="/docs/guide/audit-log">Audit log</a></li><li><a href="/docs/guide/workflows">Workflows</a></li></ul>', 21)
